{title: Grace Greater Than Our Sin}
{artist: Julia H. Johnston / Daniel B. Towner}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: G}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 3/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The United Methodist Hymnal (Nashville, Tennessee: United Methodist Publishing House, 1989), # 365)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Marvelous [D7]grace [Em]of our [G]loving Lord,
[D7]Grace that exceeds our [G]sin and our guilt!
[G]Yonder on [D7]Cal[Em]vary’s [G]mount [D7]out[Em]poured,
[Am]There where the blood of the [G]Lamb__[D]__ was [G]spilled.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Grace, grace, [C]God’s__[G]__ grace,
[D7]Grace that will pardon and [G]cleanse within;
[G]Grace, grace, [C]God’s__[G]__ grace,
[Am]Grace that is greater than [G]all__[D]__ our [G]sin.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Sin and des[D7]pair, [Em]like the [G]sea waves cold,
[D7]Threaten the soul with [G]infinite loss;
[G]Grace that is [D7]great[Em]er, yes, [G]grace [D7]un[Em]told,
[Am]Points to the refuge, the [G]might__[D]__y [G]cross.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Dark is the [D7]stain [Em]that we [G]cannot hide.
[D7]What can avail to [G]wash it away?
[G]Look! There is [D7]flow[Em]ing a [G]crim[D7]son [Em]tide,
[Am]Brighter than snow you may [G]be__[D]__ to[G]day.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Marvelous, [D7]in[Em]finite, [G]matchless grace,
[D7]Freely bestowed on [G]all who believe!
[G]You that are [D7]long[Em]ing to [G]see [D7]His [Em]face,
[Am]Will you this moment His [G]grace__[D]__ re[G]ceive?
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
